1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Twelfth Episode
The Prince and the Gypsy
Ragged Prince

15
00:02:14,563 --> 00:02:16,720
Ah, Sapphire! Good morning.

16
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:18,880
Good morning, Tink.

17
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,146
Hey, wait!

18
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,280
Who are you people?

19
00:02:36,499 --> 00:02:40,340
Please forgive my companion Gem for being so rude just now.

20
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:44,540
I'm just glad you and this gentleman weren't hurt.

21
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:48,180
Don't worry about it! As you can see—

22
00:02:48,987 --> 00:02:51,119
Ow, that hurts!

23
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,853
Unbelievable...

24
00:02:54,034 --> 00:02:58,460
Hey! How can you stand there laughing after our friend got badly hurt?!

25
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,940
Where did he go?

26
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:19,140
Huh, he's pretty strong.

27
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:20,460
Of course he is.

28
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:23,344
He's the Prince of Silverland. Wait, a prince?

29
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:25,480
He doesn't look like much for a prince.

30
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,553
You look pretty shabby yourself.

31
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:29,980
Can't be helped.

32
00:03:30,255 --> 00:03:31,706
We're gypsies, after all.

33
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,160
Gypsies?

34
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,620
What's a gypsy?

35
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:42,760
We're folks who travel all year round—singing, doing magic tricks, and stealing stuff.

36
00:03:42,904 --> 00:03:44,640
My name's Gem.

37
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:47,253
And what about your mother and father?

38
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:54,140
My mom and dad died a long time ago.

39
00:03:54,454 --> 00:03:56,180
Must be nice to be a prince.

40
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,860
Just once, I'd like to boss people around in a place like that.

41
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,340
Shall I let you?

42
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:02,780
Don't tease me.

43
00:04:03,024 --> 00:04:04,940
How could you do that just as a favor for a gypsy?

44
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,173
Oh, but I can!

45
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,100
How?

46
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,600
How's this?

47
00:04:18,405 --> 00:04:19,899
What's the point of making a face like that?

48
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,273
Wow, you two look identical!

49
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:25,440
Right now, I'm reading a book called The Prince and the Pauper.

50
00:04:26,705 --> 00:04:29,790
It's about a prince and a beggar swapping places. See?

51
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:35,026
So, just like in the book, Gypsy and I are going to swap places.

52
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,200
Great idea, right?

53
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,440
Hey, Gem!

54
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,400
I haven't even had dinner yet!

55
00:04:42,525 --> 00:04:45,900
Man, he's late. What is he doing?

56
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,840
Whoa, I can't tell which is which!

57
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:57,280
Gem, make sure you come back here by evening.

58
00:04:57,386 --> 00:04:57,786
Got it?

59
00:04:58,050 --> 00:04:59,050
Okay!

60
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,280
Well then!

61
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,700
Wait! Wait!

62
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,600
Sapphire! Wait!

63
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,820
Yahoo!

64
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:38,240
Whoa, isn't that Tink?!

65
00:05:38,410 --> 00:05:40,520
Sapphire, help me!

66
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:42,246
What are you doing here?

67
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:44,660
The town bullies caught me!

68
00:05:45,850 --> 00:05:48,360
Well, well! Are you a friend of his?

69
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:52,180
Hey! Picking on the weak isn't right!

70
00:05:52,505 --> 00:05:53,873
What?! You've got some nerve!

71
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:55,400
Where did you come from?!

72
00:05:55,510 --> 00:05:56,510
Over there!

73
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,340
All right, you weirdo!

74
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:00,860
If you want him back, you'll have to duel me!

75
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:02,820
A duel?

76
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:06,520
Come on!

77
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,840
You big neighborhood bully!

78
00:06:07,945 --> 00:06:08,945
All right, here I come!

79
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:09,980
You little brat!

80
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:15,680
Help!

81
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:28,300
How strange!

82
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,180
It's a tie!

83
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,240
Let me try again!

84
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,360
All right!

85
00:06:44,585 --> 00:06:45,720
Okay!

86
00:06:45,985 --> 00:06:47,060
Alright, watch this!

87
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,400
Here I go!

88
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,600
Yah! Hello there!

89
00:07:02,591 --> 00:07:03,153
Yah!

90
00:07:03,299 --> 00:07:05,826
I'm not... I mean, I am the Prince!

91
00:07:05,904 --> 00:07:07,066
Show some respect!

92
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,940
Uh, no, wait... hey, I know you, pal!

93
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:12,766
What's going on?

94
00:07:15,710 --> 00:07:17,386
Uh, does my voice sound strange?

95
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,480
I-I've caught a cold!

96
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,686
Help!

97
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:39,520
Sapphire, look how late it's getting...

98
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:43,480
That's right, we must head back!

99
00:07:43,845 --> 00:07:45,640
Whoa, wait for me!

100
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,306
Sapphire!

101
00:08:10,256 --> 00:08:11,356
Forgive me!

102
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,500
Water, please!

103
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,039
Stop it!

104
00:08:29,075 --> 00:08:32,200
Well now, Gem, you've got some nerve kicking me.

105
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,878
I thought your friends had abandoned you and left.

106
00:08:44,897 --> 00:08:46,971
Gem, I shall tell your fortune.

107
00:08:46,995 --> 00:08:49,170
An ill-omened star hangs over you.

108
00:08:51,579 --> 00:08:56,593
Let's see... one, five, eight... thirteen cards.

109
00:08:57,899 --> 00:08:59,713
Gem, your star is...

110
00:09:02,306 --> 00:09:03,260
This one!

111
00:09:07,529 --> 00:09:09,940
My, Gem... your card says you're a girl!

112
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,120
My, I've really gotten old.

113
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,660
I'm already dead!

114
00:09:21,139 --> 00:09:22,139
Brother Gem!

115
00:09:24,559 --> 00:09:26,040
Welcome home, Brother.

116
00:09:26,215 --> 00:09:27,620
Your dinner is over there, Brother.

117
00:09:29,145 --> 00:09:30,558
Hold it!

118
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:34,420
You didn't earn a single coin today. Got it?

119
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,460
So you're only getting half a portion.

120
00:09:36,665 --> 00:09:38,180
Remember that.

121
00:09:39,729 --> 00:09:40,633
Then, who are...

122
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:46,060
Who are you?

123
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,620
I'm Gem's sister.

124
00:09:49,915 --> 00:09:51,440
I won't tell anyone, so please tell me.

125
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:52,675
Where is my brother?

126
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,880
Is he not coming back?

127
00:09:54,439 --> 00:09:57,980
Well, for various reasons, I swapped places with your brother.

128
00:09:58,365 --> 00:10:00,120
I am the prince of Silverland.

129
00:10:00,469 --> 00:10:02,180
Wow, so you're a prince!

130
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,460
It's Liz, the little bird.

131
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,520
Liz, you've come back too?

132
00:10:06,695 --> 00:10:08,060
It's already evening, isn't it?

133
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Oh no!

134
00:10:10,689 --> 00:10:12,393
It's gotten so dark already.

135
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:16,199
Hurry, or it'll get dark.

136
00:10:17,019 --> 00:10:18,259
Ah, Gem!

137
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,440
Hey, Tink!

138
00:10:24,279 --> 00:10:25,860
The castle is so boring.

139
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:35,280
Must be nice.

140
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:38,280
This is the last of the potion that reveals whether Sapphire is a boy or a girl.

141
00:10:38,635 --> 00:10:40,140
Make no mistakes this time, men!

142
00:10:40,569 --> 00:10:45,340
Coat your blade with it. It turns blue on a man, and red on a woman.

143
00:10:45,535 --> 00:10:47,180
And bright yellow on an egg!

144
00:10:49,345 --> 00:10:50,598
Attack!

145
00:10:51,413 --> 00:10:52,413
Intruders!

146
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,433
Stand back!

147
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,106
Stand back!

148
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,340
I am the Prince!

149
00:10:58,439 --> 00:11:00,513
And it's the Prince we have business with!

150
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:02,813
We got him!

151
00:11:02,838 --> 00:11:03,806
We did it!

152
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,540
Curse it!

153
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,100
We haven't searched here yet!

154
00:11:14,529 --> 00:11:17,360
Have no fear, it is Nylon. I've driven off the intruder.

155
00:11:17,514 --> 00:11:18,806
Please, lift your head.

156
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:19,960
Is that so?

157
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,180
He's a man!

158
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,880
What are you talking about? Of course I'm a man!

159
00:11:49,939 --> 00:11:51,760
Come, Gem is waiting. Let's hurry!

160
00:12:01,688 --> 00:12:03,000
No, no, Gem.

161
00:12:03,255 --> 00:12:05,340
You won't escape that easily!

162
00:12:05,675 --> 00:12:07,553
Drag them all away!

163
00:12:13,749 --> 00:12:15,540
Nylon, say that again!

164
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:16,733
Yes, my lord.

165
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,639
So Prince Sapphire really is a boy...

166
00:12:20,403 --> 00:12:23,500
Nonsense! That fool's potion must have failed!

167
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:25,940
No, no, Lord Duralumin.

168
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:30,441
The potion's effect will never fail, even if the sun rises in the west. Indeed.

169
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,720
How can this be?!

170
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:35,100
To think Sapphire was a boy all along!

171
00:12:36,305 --> 00:12:37,305
Hey, Nylon!

172
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:38,059
Yes, Sir.

173
00:12:38,289 --> 00:12:40,591
In that case, our last resort is to kill Sapphire...

174
00:12:40,615 --> 00:12:42,306
Kill him... Yes.

175
00:12:43,599 --> 00:12:46,040
But those three assassins aren't enough.

176
00:12:46,345 --> 00:12:48,680
You've tamed the Gypsies, haven't you?

177
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:01,120
No!

178
00:13:01,625 --> 00:13:02,859
I wasn't trying to run away!

179
00:13:03,235 --> 00:13:05,846
I intended to bring back the real Gem!

180
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:11,620
I'm a prince!

181
00:13:12,235 --> 00:13:14,640
If you think I'm lying, bring anyone you want from the castle!

182
00:13:15,395 --> 00:13:16,395
A prince?

183
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:18,360
Hey, did you all hear that?

184
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:20,300
Gem's finally lost his mind!

185
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:24,200
What if it's true?!

186
00:13:30,166 --> 00:13:30,973
Stop laughing!

187
00:13:31,045 --> 00:13:31,659
t's not a lie!

188
00:13:36,775 --> 00:13:37,860
Please, Mr. Ton.

189
00:13:37,885 --> 00:13:39,440
Please forgive my brother!

190
00:13:40,415 --> 00:13:41,555
Forgive him?

191
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:43,680
He's got some nerve!

192
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:47,180
Trying to run away when he doesn't even earn his keep—I can't stand it!

193
00:13:47,825 --> 00:13:50,320
Then I'll work in his place!

194
00:13:50,786 --> 00:13:51,980
Work?

195
00:13:52,005 --> 00:13:53,220
Well, fair enough.

196
00:13:53,410 --> 00:13:55,200
Alright, I'll give you a job.

197
00:13:55,345 --> 00:13:56,740
Hey, cut Pepper's ropes!

198
00:13:58,719 --> 00:14:00,780
Take this bundle to town and sell it!

199
00:14:01,026 --> 00:14:01,420
What?

200
00:14:01,572 --> 00:14:02,718
Right now?

201
00:14:03,546 --> 00:14:07,093
That's right! If you sell it all by dawn, I'll spare Gem!

202
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:09,040
That's insane!

203
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:10,766
Who's going to buy anything this late?!

204
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:13,560
If you fail, he gets hanged!

205
00:14:21,589 --> 00:14:23,980
Wait for me, Brother! I promise I'll sell it all!

206
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:25,920
Pepper!

207
00:15:20,041 --> 00:15:25,750
I'm scared, Father... Brother...

208
00:15:40,229 --> 00:15:41,229
Here's the town...

209
00:15:50,659 --> 00:15:53,675
Would anyone like some firewood?

210
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:54,580
No, thanks.

211
00:15:57,529 --> 00:15:59,276
Would anyone like some firewood?

212
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,520
Would anyone like some...

213
00:16:15,869 --> 00:16:16,746
My firewood...

214
00:16:22,089 --> 00:16:23,680
I need to gather it fast!

215
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:32,240
Help!

216
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,526
Help!

217
00:16:41,004 --> 00:16:42,318
Help!

218
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,665
A girl is drowning!

219
00:16:46,689 --> 00:16:48,740
Help!

220
00:16:55,614 --> 00:16:58,587
Goro-goro-san Come on, come on, quickly!

221
00:17:10,169 --> 00:17:12,526
Goro-goro-san thank you!

222
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,360
Sister!

223
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,159
Father

224
00:17:51,929 --> 00:17:52,929
Mother!

225
00:18:35,839 --> 00:18:36,860
Open your eyes!

226
00:18:39,779 --> 00:18:41,400
Don't... don't die!

227
00:18:41,474 --> 00:18:43,000
After I went through all the trouble to save you!

228
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:46,720
Please!

229
00:18:46,824 --> 00:18:48,200
Save this child!

230
00:18:54,665 --> 00:18:56,140
What about that Heavenly Father?

231
00:18:56,539 --> 00:18:57,660
At least say something!

232
00:18:58,460 --> 00:18:59,460
Ah!

233
00:19:18,099 --> 00:19:19,099
It's beautiful!

234
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:21,420
It's gold!

235
00:19:22,389 --> 00:19:24,960
Mother must have given it to me in my dream!

236
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:26,960
Thank you!

237
00:19:30,349 --> 00:19:31,349
Good for you!

238
00:19:35,830 --> 00:19:36,830
Hey, Jim!

239
00:19:36,949 --> 00:19:38,580
Pepper isn't back yet!

240
00:19:38,903 --> 00:19:42,039
If they're not back by dawn, it's the gallows!

241
00:19:52,205 --> 00:19:53,205
Mr. Ton

242
00:19:54,825 --> 00:19:55,825
Pepper!

243
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,180
Look!

244
00:20:02,950 --> 00:20:03,720
Hey, everyone!

245
00:20:03,879 --> 00:20:04,960
This is gold!

246
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,260
Hey!

247
00:20:06,529 --> 00:20:07,640
I'll cut Gem's rope!

248
00:20:09,929 --> 00:20:11,395
Pepper!

249
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:14,355
Hey!

250
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:15,013
Gypsy scum!

251
00:20:15,195 --> 00:20:16,195
This looks important!

252
00:20:16,325 --> 00:20:17,325
Oh boy, oh boy!

253
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,360
Lord Officers!

254
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,820
If it's official castle business!

255
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,060
Then hear my command!

256
00:20:21,549 --> 00:20:22,700
Kill Sapphire!

257
00:20:23,169 --> 00:20:24,520
By order of the castle... for me?

258
00:20:25,489 --> 00:20:28,200
First, Sapphire goes for a walk with Lord Nylon!

259
00:20:28,819 --> 00:20:29,819
That's when we kill him!

260
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:30,700
Ton!

261
00:20:31,259 --> 00:20:32,540
Go get four men at once!

262
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:33,980
Got it!

263
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:35,920
Yah!

264
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,820
Thank you for your service!

265
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,040
Hey!

266
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,260
Everyone, assemble!

267
00:20:41,530 --> 00:20:42,530
Let us do this together!

268
00:20:43,329 --> 00:20:44,760
Men, this is official castle business!

269
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:45,860
Stay sharp!

270
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:48,220
Oh no!

271
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:49,560
Gem is in danger!

272
00:20:49,824 --> 00:20:51,020
Please, Highness!

273
00:20:51,214 --> 00:20:52,380
Save my big brother!

274
00:20:53,649 --> 00:20:55,280
If Big Brother dies, Pepper will die too!

275
00:21:00,459 --> 00:21:01,680
Oh, Lil!

276
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:02,920
All right!

277
00:21:02,990 --> 00:21:03,990
Do not worry, Pepper!

278
00:21:04,234 --> 00:21:06,340
I, Sapphire, will surely save your brother!

279
00:21:06,341 --> 00:21:07,341
Please!

280
00:21:30,089 --> 00:21:33,780
A morning ride truly is delightful, Your Highness.

281
00:21:33,919 --> 00:21:36,406
It is an honor to accompany you.

282
00:21:36,749 --> 00:21:39,966
Honor is fine, but slow down a bit!

283
00:21:42,879 --> 00:21:45,260
Let us head back to the castle now.

284
00:21:50,639 --> 00:21:52,180
He always rushes off like that.

285
00:21:52,499 --> 00:21:53,700
He went the wrong way!

286
00:21:59,590 --> 00:22:01,146
Help!

287
00:22:04,269 --> 00:22:05,269
Prince!

288
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:06,620
Help me!

289
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:26,580
Gem!

290
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:27,180
I'm coming!

291
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:28,260
He's here!

292
00:22:28,740 --> 00:22:29,740
- Your Highness!
- Gem

293
00:22:30,409 --> 00:22:31,409
Keep out of my way!

294
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:37,706
Wait, aren't you Gem?!

295
00:22:37,824 --> 00:22:39,540
What on earth are you doing here?!

296
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,180
Go back!

297
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:41,280
Get out of here!

298
00:22:41,539 --> 00:22:44,680
I'm sorry, but I can't go back!

299
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,980
Your Highness really is strong.

300
00:23:20,759 --> 00:23:22,400
Gem, what about the assassins?

301
00:23:22,769 --> 00:23:25,400
That pole hit them earlier, so they're knocked out cold over there.

302
00:23:31,959 --> 00:23:33,500
Gem, did you enjoy yourself?

303
00:23:33,580 --> 00:23:34,580
Inside the castle?

304
00:23:35,774 --> 00:23:37,960
It was totally boring in there.

305
00:23:38,214 --> 00:23:39,440
There were always guards watching me.

306
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:40,720
How about you, Sapphire?

307
00:23:41,209 --> 00:23:43,680
A lot happened on my end, too.

308
00:23:44,274 --> 00:23:47,140
I feel I learned quite a lot from it all.

309
00:23:51,229 --> 00:23:52,229
Farewell, Gem.

310
00:23:52,479 --> 00:23:53,500
Pepper is waiting for you.

311
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:54,499
Yeah.

312
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:00,840
Damn it!

313
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:02,460
That prince was an imposter!

314
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,853
Damn it!

315
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:05,720
He's an imposter!

316
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:06,140
An imposter!

317
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:06,620
An imposter!

318
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:07,660
An imposter!

319
00:24:54,739 --> 00:25:01,300
Though demons come or storms may rage, our joined hearts will never part.

320
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:32,500
Good night. Good night.

